    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nBracketed\n\n### Description\n\nRight now you can just use descrete diagnostic levels like 'warning' or 'error'. It would be great to have a smart option that prioritized errors, then if the file doesnt contain any errors goes for warnings. \r\n\r\nWhenever i use goto diagnostics in a file with an error i have to go through many warnings until i get there. However if I set the severity level to \"Error\", I can no longer go to warnings. I think this smart option to prioritize errors would be a great middle ground ",
