    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nI don't think this is a good fit for 'mini.bracketed' mostly because it goes against how diagnostic navigation is done in built-in `vim.diagnostic.goto_{next,prev}()`. The `vim.diagnostic.goto_{next,prev}_pos()` functions are used directly in `diagnostic` target. Implementing custom logic would mean complicating code.\r\n\r\nIn this situation I would suggest to make different extra mappings to jump to a specific level entry. Maybe something like `]e` to jump to next error, etc.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
